{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ACT",
  "chapter": 18,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After these things, Paul departed from Athens, and came to Corinth;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And found a certain Jew named Aquila, born in Pontus, lately come from Italy, with his wife Priscilla (because that Claudius had commanded all Jews to depart from Rome) and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " came to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And because he was of the same occupation, he abode with them, and wrought (for by their occupation they were tent-makers)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he reasoned in the synagogue every sabbath, and persuaded the Jews and the Greeks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when Silas and Timothy had come from Macedonia, Paul was pressed in spirit, and testified to the Jews, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Jesus ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they opposed themselves, and blasphemed, he shook ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " raiment, and said to them, Your blood ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon your own heads: I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " clean: from henceforth I will go to the Gentiles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he departed thence, and entered into the house of a certain man named Justus, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that worshiped God, whose house joined close to the synagogue.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Crispus the chief ruler of the synagogue believed on the Lord with all his house: and many of the Corinthians hearing, believed, and were baptized.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the Lord spoke to Paul in the night by a vision, Be not afraid, but speak, and hold not thy peace:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I am with thee, and no man shall lay hands on thee, to hurt thee: for I have many people in this city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he continued ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a year and six months, teaching the word of God among them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when Gallio was the deputy of Achaia, the Jews made insurrection with one accord against Paul, and brought him to the judgment-seat,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Saying, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " persuadeth men to worship God contrary to the law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when Paul was now about to open ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mouth, Gallio said to the Jews, If it were a matter of wrong, or hainous crime, O ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ye",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Jews, reason would that I should bear with you:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if it is a question of words and names, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " your law, look ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": for I will be no judge of such ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "matters",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he drove them from the judgment-seat.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then all the Greeks took Sosthenes, the chief ruler of the synagogue, and beat ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before the judgment-seat. And Gallio cared for none of those things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Paul ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "after this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " tarried ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yet a good while, and took his leave of the brethren, and sailed thence into Syria, and with him Priscilla and Aquila; having shorn ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " head in Cenchrea: for he had a vow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he came to Ephesus, and left them there: but he himself entered into the synagogue, and reasoned with the Jews.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When they desired ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to tarry longer time with them, he consented not:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But bade them farewell, saying, I must by all means keep this feast that cometh in Jerusalem: but I will return to you, if God will. And he sailed from Ephesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he had landed at Cesarea, and gone up and saluted the church, he went down to Antioch.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And after he had spent some time ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", he departed and went over ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "all",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the country of Galatia and Phrygia in order, strengthening all the disciples.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And a certain Jew named Apollos, born at Alexandria, an eloquent man, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mighty in the scriptures, came to Ephesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This man was instructed in the way of the Lord: and being fervent in the spirit, he spoke and taught diligently the things of the Lord, knowing only the baptism of John.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he began to speak boldly in the synagogue: Whom, when Aquila and Priscilla had heard, they took him to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and expounded to him the way of God more perfectly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he was disposed to pass into Achaia, the brethren wrote, exhorting the disciples to receive him: who, when he had come, helped them much who had believed through grace.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ACT.18.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ACT.18.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he mightily convinced the Jews, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " publicly, showing by the scriptures, that Jesus was Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
